evals/results/

# RepoRadar generated output (local runs)
/reporadar_digest.*
/digests/
# The paper store `rr init` creates. Generated state, binary, and it grows every
# run (2.6 MB after one run of this repo), so it never belongs in a commit.
# The trailing slash restricts the match to the directory: a bare `/.reporadar`
# would also swallow a stray *file* of that name. It is NOT needed to protect the
# committed `.reporadar.yml` beside it — gitignore matches whole path components,
# so neither form touches that file. Both checked with `git check-ignore`.
/.reporadar/
# Scratch configs for pointing `rr` at a benchmark clone (`diffusion.reporadar.yml`
# and friends). They carry absolute machine-specific paths, so they must not be
# committed by a stray `git add -A`.
# The leading `?` is load-bearing: gitignore's `*` matches the empty string, so
# `/*.reporadar.yml` would also hide a user's real `.reporadar.yml` — verified.
/?*.reporadar.yml

# PyPI configuration file
.pypirc

# Cursor
#  Cursor is an AI-powered code editor. `.cursorignore` specifies files/directories to
#  exclude from AI features like autocomplete and code analysis. Recommended for sensitive data
#  refer to https://docs.cursor.com/context/ignore-files
.cursorignore
.cursorindexingignore

# Marimo
marimo/_static/
marimo/_lsp/
__marimo__/

# The pool enumeration keeps its full raw API responses locally: ~250 MB across ~500 files,
# and every payload carries html_url for every repository -- the exact `github.com/<owner>/<repo>`
# pattern PREREG-judge-validity-pool.md section 2.1 keeps out of this tree. The committed record
# is the trimmed archive beside it, which preserves query, Date, total_count and returned names.
evals/frame/pool/raw/

# T0 judge prompts. They are README excerpts, so they carry OTHER repositories' URLs
# (measured: graph 2, rag 3) -- the github.com/<owner>/<repo> pattern section 2.1 keeps out of
# this tree. They are working files, not datasheet artefacts: section 10 step 7 publishes the
# ledger, positives, controls and verdicts, and each row already carries its context HASH,
# which is what makes the prompt verifiable without publishing the prompt.
evals/frame/pool/contexts/
